**Lyasoff (2016), p. 1071–1073, Theorem 4.1 (PDE part)**

hypothesis that a candidate φc satisfies the first-order
   transport PDE along V. `theorem_4_1_pde` is the conditional rearrangement;
   `cond_density_satisfies_theorem_41_pde` establishes the hypothesis for a
   conditional density of exp-BM.


**Lyasoff (2016), p. 1073, Theorem 4.1 identity (4.4) (Donati-Martin–Matsumoto–Yor)**

hypothesis for the reciprocal-moment cases
   E[(∫ e^{σW})^{-1} | W_t = y/σ] = y/(t(e^y−1)) (and 1/t at y=0).
   PAPER NOTE: printed ∫₀ᵗ should be ∫₀^∞ x^{-1} φ(x|·) dx.
   `theorem_4_1_striking` is the conditional rearrangement;
   `cond_density_satisfies_striking` establishes the hypothesis for a
   conditional density.


**Lyasoff (2016), p. 1074, ODE along each line**

derivative of exp(−u/2 − (4/x) cosh(u/2)).
   PAPER NOTE: printed sinh sign is wrong; the consistent sign is minus.


**Lyasoff (2016), p. 1075–1076, formula (4.6). Conditional rearrangement assuming `SatisfiesFoliationODE`**


**Lyasoff (2016), Remark 4.3 / Laplace transform of the conditional law of A_t^{-1}**

L_{t,y}(u) = ∫ e^{-u/x} φ(x|y) dx.


**Lyasoff (2016), p. 1077, operator T_{t,y}**

the transform used to characterize the Laplace transform uniquely.


**Lyasoff (2016), p. 1077, Proposition 4.4. The paper invokes uniqueness of the Laplace transform; measurability and integrability are the missing hypotheses in the informal statement**


**Lyasoff (2016), p. 1078, Theorem 4.5. Conditional closed form for the Laplace transform via arcosh, assuming `TransformedMassIdentity` and `HasLaplaceReduction`**


**Lyasoff (2016), corollary of Thm 4.5 recovering (4.4)**

differentiating the Laplace closed form yields the striking identity.


**Lyasoff (2016), p. 1079, negative moments at y = 0 (first few)**

Taylor expansion of L_{t,0}(u) gives E[A_t^{-p} | W_t=0].


**Lyasoff (2016), Remark 4.6**

the striking identity is the p = 1 case of the negative-moment formulae.
